cff-version: 1.2.0
title: Arginine Dose Response in Hypertension
message: If you use this analysis, please cite it as below.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Hatem
    given-names: Hossam
    affiliation: Nile University
  - family-names: Mohamed
    given-names: Aseel
    affiliation: Nile University
  - family-names: Elsayed
    given-names: May
    affiliation: Nile University
abstract: >-
  A reproducible statistical analysis of a dose-finding trial in which 40
  hypertensive patients were randomised across four daily doses of arginine
  (0, 2, 5 and 10 mg) and systolic blood pressure reduction was measured after
  two months. Covers descriptive statistics, assumption testing, confidence
  intervals, hypothesis testing with post-hoc comparison, and linear modelling.
  Finds a linear dose response of 1.79 mmHg per mg/day and a significant
  dose-by-sex interaction that an additive model does not detect.
keywords:
  - statistics
  - R
  - dose-response
  - hypertension
  - ANOVA
  - linear-regression
  - reproducible-research
